     "text": "In 1889 came the first Yiddish political cartoon, depicting a chicken with the head of Tsar Alexander, referring to the Jewish custom of kaporus, involving swinging a decapitated chicken over one\u2019s head before Passover. The Hebrew Puck (or Yiddishe Puck) reprinted cartoons from other magazines, but ",
